Enhancement: Verify a large blob without a second copy of it in memory

Before a blob is uploaded, restic decrypts and decompresses it again and checks
that it still hashes to the same value, which catches corruption from faulty
memory or a software bug. For a large blob that check decompressed the whole
thing into memory a second time, doubling what the blob cost while it was being
saved. The tree of a directory with a million entries runs to several hundred
megabytes, so this was enough to push a memory-capped host over the edge.

Blobs above 16 MiB are now hashed as they decompress, so verification no longer
depends on the blob's size. Nothing about what is verified has changed.

